{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"a49398ba517c971d6be079055941bd1905f118ac7076fa2f5e3940e71940b9b2","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_6f10f07e086e5358ce20c2b64aaedda6c11a47703682507f18b52a4ce23d0cf4","overall_assessment":"The paper demonstrates high clarity in writing, notation, and visual presentation. The methods are well-explained with clear algorithms and consistent mathematical definitions. Figures and tables are informative and well-labeled, supporting the reader's understanding of the proposed techniques and results. Minor terminology inconsistencies do not significantly impact the overall clarity.","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_identity_sha256":"8a99c61674a62834e221216229c615b33150c873b663930293dd5b821f155fe7","prompt_identity_sha256":"58527c9934d3e6a28b4c3b545b9407a5d5409b891ad623c3e78ad26210064996","raw_response_sha256":"ac80d18b791b2f8566b5176330c30e23032e958c2e672f6edf6986652a41459f","request_identity_sha256":"b5c3ff5adc40f316e558c6b952c6ca5a2a7a39effc36ca7f872fda6ca8f2d825","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-007","SRC-012","SRC-020","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The paper is well-organized with a logical flow from introduction to method, results, and related work. The writing is generally clear and concise, effectively explaining the core concept of self-ensembling. The algorithm presentations (Algorithm 1 and 2) are self-contained, with clear inputs, outputs, and step-by-step logic, aided by helpful comments. However, there is a minor inconsistency in terminology where the 'II-model' is sometimes referred to as 'Pi-model' (e.g., in Section 3.4 and Figure 2 caption), which could cause slight confusion. Additionally, the explanation of the 'dark knowledge' concept in Section 2.1 could be slightly more explicit for readers unfamiliar with knowledge distillation, though the citation is provided.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-011","SRC-013"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. Key variables such as $x_i$, $y_i$, $z_i$, $\\tilde{z}_i$, $Z_i$, and $\\alpha$ are clearly introduced in Section 2 and used consistently throughout the text and algorithms. The derivation of the bias correction term $(1 - \\alpha^t)$ in temporal ensembling is explained clearly, linking it to similar techniques in Adam and batch normalization. The loss function components are explicitly defined in both the text and the pseudocode, ensuring clarity for reproduction. No significant gaps or inconsistencies in notation were found.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-020","SRC-024"],"review_text":"Figure 1 provides a clear structural overview of the two methods, with distinct top and bottom panels for the Pi-model and temporal ensembling, respectively. The caption effectively explains the role of labels and loss components. Figure 2 illustrates the tolerance to incorrect labels, with a clear comparison between standard supervised training and the Pi-model. The tables (Table 1, 2, and 3) are well-structured, with clear headers and consistent formatting for error rates and standard deviations. Table 3 provides a detailed and legible description of the network architecture, aiding reproducibility. All visual aids are properly labeled and contribute significantly to understanding the methods and results.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"8a97a865533ee010cb3410e64f69dc5e5ea11824b3a6b10148bbe15bdf482a01","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_ordinal":21,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"ac80d18b791b2f8566b5176330c30e23032e958c2e672f6edf6